# Classes, students, clients, and custom orders

This is a core part of vitrify.

vitrify must support atelier work that is not only anonymous stock production.

A professional ceramic atelier often manages several overlapping production contexts:

* pieces made for general stock
* pieces made for a custom client order
* pieces made during a class or workshop
* pieces belonging to a student
* pieces brought in by a student or client
* test pieces or one-off experiments
* replacement pieces made because an earlier piece failed

These contexts are not decorative side features.

They are part of the core product model because they explain why a physical piece exists and who or what it belongs to.

The website must make this value clear in plain, elegant language.

A ceramist should immediately understand that vitrify can help answer questions like:

* Which student pieces still need firing?
* Which class pieces are ready to return?
* Which pieces belong to this custom order?
* What failed in this order?
* What needs to be remade?
* Which client pieces are ready but not yet delivered?
* Which external or brought-in pieces are in the kiln queue?
* What is actual available stock, and what is already reserved?

